    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NswrB4bSkiQMXwFuMJXv4Z)_\n\n## Cause\n`sp-bibliography-dir` was `(sp-paths--dir sp-documents-dir \"bibliography/\")`, but the first argument of `sp-paths--dir` is an environment variable *name*. `getenv` returned nil, so the folder became `bibliography/` below `default-directory`, which does not exist. `sp-bibtex-files` was then nil and `citar-bibliography` empty, hence `citar-select-refs: No bibliography set`. (`sp-bibtex-dir` no longer exists since #92; `sp-bibliography-dir` is the only option.)\n\n## Fix\n`(sp-paths--dir \"SP_BIBLIOGRAPHY_DIR\" (sp-path sp-documents-dir \"bibliography/\"))`: the env var, else `bibliography/` below `sp-documents-dir`, as the `sp-academic` doc already said. Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). After updating, run `C-c w b r` (`sp-bibtex-register`) or restart; the folder must contain `.bib` files whose names start with a letter or digit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAdt8amQYKFvPPhzbg)_",
